From dd4a0b4396c4365bfac20d5f19c4ed97cf15c73a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krishna Kurapati <krishna.kurapati@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 15:10:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 053/165] phy: qualcomm: phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater: Fix SMB Power
 leakage issue

On Glymur, it is observed that although the exit call is done, there is a
power leakage seen on SMB2370 charger (which embeds the eUSB2 module as
well). As per recommendation of HW team, disable the repeater during the
exit call to prevent this power leakage.

Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Krishna Kurapati <krishna.kurapati@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
[ upsync: patchwork 14824745, posted to linux-arm-msm/linux-phy 2026-09-17, not yet in phy/next ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c
index d056f0f8dd93..724b64d5f192 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-eusb2-repeater.c
@@ -230,7 +230,9 @@ static int eusb2_repeater_set_mode(struct phy *phy,
 static int eusb2_repeater_exit(struct phy *phy)
 {
 	struct eusb2_repeater *rptr = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+	struct regmap *regmap = rptr->regmap;
 
+	regmap_write(regmap, EUSB2_EN_CTL1, 0);
 	return regulator_bulk_disable(rptr->cfg->num_vregs, rptr->vregs);
 }
 
